1-3. `renderOrder` inside the material constructor options — in three's type definitions, `renderOrder` is not a property of the material (it's a property of Object3D!). That's right — `renderOrder` belongs to `Object3D`, not `Material`. In other words, setting `renderOrder` in the LineBasicMaterial/MeshBasicMaterial constructor options is invalid both type-wise and at runtime (it just sets an unused property on the material instance; the renderer uses object.renderOrder). Fix: remove `renderOrder` from the material options and set `line.renderOrder = FLASH_RENDER_ORDER; spark.renderOrder = FLASH_RENDER_ORDER; flash.renderOrder = FLASH_RENDER_ORDER;` on the objects instead.

